    <briefdescription>
<para>Non-linear least-square method. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Using a given optimization algorithm (default is conjugate gradient),</para><para><formula id="228">\[ min \{ r(x) : x in R^n \} \]</formula> <verbatim>  where \form#229 is the Euclidean norm of \form#230@_fakenl for some vector-valued function \form#37 from
</verbatim> <formula id="231">$ R^n $</formula> to <formula id="232">$ R^m $</formula>, <formula id="233">\[ f = (f_1, ..., f_m) \]</formula> with <formula id="234">$ f_i(x) = b_i - \phi(x,t_i) $</formula> where <formula id="48">$ b $</formula> is the vector of target data and <formula id="235">$ phi $</formula> is a scalar function.</para><para>Assuming the differentiability of <formula id="37">$ f $</formula>, the gradient of <formula id="65">$ r $</formula> is defined by <formula id="236">\[ grad r(x) = f&apos;(x)^t.f(x) \]</formula> </para>    </detaileddescription>
